# Trivy suppressions for rocCV.
# Reference: https://trivy.dev/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/#trivyignore
#
# Picked up from the repository root by the shared security-baseline
# workflow (ROCm/rocm-security-gh) and passed to trivy via --ignorefile.
# Every entry needs a reason and a condition for removing it.

# lxml 5.2.1 (docs/sphinx/requirements.txt): local file read via external
# entities when parsing untrusted XML, fixed in lxml 6.1.0.
#
# Cannot be bumped: doxysphinx 3.3.14, the latest release, pins
# lxml<=5.2.1. The bound was relaxed upstream in boschglobal/doxysphinx#182
# but has not been released yet (tracked in boschglobal/doxysphinx#188).
#
# Not exploitable here: lxml is only used by doxysphinx during the docs
# build, to parse Doxygen XML generated from this repository's own headers.
# No untrusted XML is ever parsed, and nothing ships in libroccv or rocpycv.
#
# Remove once a doxysphinx release allows lxml>=6.1.0, and bump both in
# docs/sphinx/requirements.txt.
CVE-2026-41066
